262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (We also encountered contradictions across studies. Some sources, for example, suggest that social media has significantly reduced young people's ability to concentrate, while others show more nuanced patterns, including young people who actively regulate their own screen use. These differences remind us that many of the claims about generations remain debated and are not always supported by strong evidence. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E ( The most reliable insights for our work with young people will always come from listening directly to them. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Another limitation is that the voices of young people, especially Gen Alpha, are still relatively underrepresented in research. Many studies rely on observations by adults rather than direct participation from the young people themselves. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
