endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Gen Z is influencing education, work, consumption, and civic engagement. Born into a highly connected digital environment, shaped by social media, algorithms, and constant information, they experience the world differently from previous generations. Understanding these factors can help educators and organisations engage more effectively with this generation. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Gen Z's educational expectations are driven by practicality and perceived meaning. Students are increasingly choosing studies based on occupation ability, job stability, and personal interests rather than social prestige alone. They want education programmes to offer transferable skills and that have a clear use in their career paths. In higher education, students are increasingly becoming aware of ethics, social responsibility, and sustainability. They also tend to favour experiential and work-based learning environments. A range of educational practices, including immersive simulations and virtual reality reinforce engagement by identifying the learner as relevant to their surroundings. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
