301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 141 0 R
/E (Gen Z's values are also visible in their consumption habits. Sustainability often matters to them, but practical factors like price and brand trust remain important. They tend to react quickly to perceived greenwashing and may withdraw support from companies they see as inauthentic. Many show interest in local, ethical, and experience-based consumption, where personal meaning and empathy play a role. This suggests that sustainability messages are more effective when they connect to everyday life rather than relying on abstract environmental language. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
