/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Gen Alpha have more access to more information than any other generation gone before and are the most globally connected generation ever. They use their devices for the gamification of education. They view digital devices as a normal and necessary means to interact with the world. However, there is little to no education on how to use their devices healthily. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Around two in five Gen Alpha gamers want to play video games that facilitate creativity and allow them to build or create. For example, Minecraft and Roblox. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (There are fears that they will experience an oral communication deficit and a loss of critical thinking skills because of a reliance on influencers for information, news and current events. Many Gen Alphas trust influencers as much as family. Social media is becoming, for many, integral to their identity development, they actively engage on websites, upload YouTube videos, and interact online with other people their age. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
