880 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (overgeneralisations about Gen Z or Gen Alpha and knowing the young people in front of you. Many practitioners describe their best learning moments as mutual - where they learn from the young people too. Saying "I'm curious about how you see this", builds trust and respect, and bridges any generational gaps. This requires accepting that young people often understand aspects of the digital and social world better than you, and valuing their knowledge as legitimate, not just "youth culture." )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
