/E (Technology is a natural part of young people's lives. Many practitioners use digital and online tools to support learning and communication. This can increase participation, especially for quieter learners. Rather than simply adopting or rejecting digital tools, you can start by reflecting about technology's role in learning and in young people's lives. Being "on track" with new generations means learning with technology, not just using it. Thus, useful questions for your own learning might be: )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [8]
>>
